<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Kinematics: velocity and maximum height of a stone (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A stone is thrown vertically upwards from a point \( {@s0@} \) m above the ground. Its height above the ground after \( t \) seconds is</p>
\[ s(t) = {@st@} \quad \text{metres}. \]
<p>(a) Find the velocity function \( v(t) \).</p>
<div>\( v(t) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) At what time does the stone reach its maximum height?</p>
<div>\( t = \) [[input:ans2]] s [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Find the maximum height.</p>
<div>Maximum height \( = \) [[input:ans3]] m [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(d) Find the velocity of the stone at \( t = {@tq@} \) s, and describe its motion at that moment.</p>
<div>\( v({@tq@}) = \) [[input:ans4]] m/s [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>
<div>At \( t = {@tq@} \) s the stone is [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Velocity is the derivative of position: \( v(t) = s'(t) = {@vt@} \) m/s.</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> At the highest point the stone is momentarily at rest, so \( v(t) = 0 \):</p>
\[ {@vt@} = 0 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad t = {@tp@} \text{ s}. \]
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( s({@tp@}) = {@s0@} + {@uu@}({@tp@}) - 5({@tp@})^2 = {@hmax@} \) m.</p>
<p><strong>(d)</strong> \( v({@tq@}) = {@uu@} - 10({@tq@}) = {@vq@} \) m/s. Upwards is the positive direction, so a positive velocity means the stone is moving upwards and a negative velocity means it is moving downwards. Its speed at that moment is \( {@abs(vq)@} \) m/s.</p>
<p>Remember: \( s(t) \) tells you <em>where</em> the stone is; \( v(t) = s'(t) \) tells you <em>how fast and in which direction</em> it is moving.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>5</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
